# Commit Discipline

Before creating any git commit in this repo:

1. Verify the local commit-msg hook is wired. If `git config core.hooksPath` does not return `.githooks`, run `make setup` (or `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`) before committing. Never run `git commit --no-verify`.
2. Format every commit message header as [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/):

   ```
   <type>(<optional scope>)!: <subject>

   <optional body>

   <optional footers>
   ```

   Allowed types: `build`, `chore`, `ci`, `docs`, `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `refactor`, `revert`, `style`, `test`. Scope is lower-case. `!` marks a breaking change. Subject is required and non-empty.

3. Do not add AI/tool attribution (e.g. "made with Cursor", "Co-authored-by: Cursor"); see `no-ai-attribution.mdc`.

```
# BAD
update stuff

added the git client

# GOOD
feat(git): add typed accessors for git config

Wraps `git config --get` with a typed accessor so callers do not have to
parse stdout. Uses the fake runner under test.
```

If a commit you are about to create would fail [`scripts/check-commit-msg.sh`](scripts/check-commit-msg.sh), rewrite the message before invoking `git commit`. The CI workflow `commitlint.yml` will reject the PR otherwise.
